, Japan, Hong Kong, Germany, Singapore, Canada, and internationally. It offers Toggle MRAM, spin-transfer torque MRAM, and tunnel magneto resistance sensor products, as well as foundry services for MRAM products and magnetic tunnel junction (MTJ)-based sensors. The company provides its products for applications, including industrial, medical, automotive/transportation, aerospace, defense, and data center markets. It serves original equipment manufacturers, contract manufacturers, and original design manufacturers through a direct sales channel, and a network of representatives and distributors. Everspin Technologies, Inc. was incorporated in 2008 and is headquartered in Chandler, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Sanjeev  Aggarwal Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 85 people. Revenue per employee of $649K ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $37K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $68K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Everspin Technologies, Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $221M market cap on $55M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -3% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +5.1pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 41% against a 12% cost of capital \u2014 a 29-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 53% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $3M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 6 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 93\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 10% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 5.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 260% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":2.604724387321352},{"text":"Operating margins 19% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $9.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 693% d